# EDM-ARS settings read from the environment.
#
# Copy this file to .env in the same folder and fill in what you use:
#   macOS / Linux:       cp .env.example .env
#   Windows PowerShell:  Copy-Item .env.example .env
#
# THIS FILE IS TRACKED BY GIT. Never put a real key here; put it in .env,
# which is gitignored. Variables already set in your shell win over .env.
#
# Leave a key empty if you do not use that service. An empty value counts
# as "not set"; a placeholder such as "your-key-here" would be sent to the
# service as if it were a real key.

# --- AI provider: the key for the provider named by llm_provider in
# config.yaml. DeepSeek is the default.
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Literature search (optional, recommended). Without a key Semantic
# Scholar is used anonymously from a shared pool that is often rate-limited.
# Request a key: https://www.semanticscholar.org/product/api#api-key-form
SEMANTIC_SCHOLAR_API_KEY=

# --- The settings below are paths, addresses or URLs. They stay commented
# out: remove the leading "# " only when you give a value. An empty
# OPENAI_BASE_URL would make the OpenAI client call an empty address, and
# an empty LSAR_HOME would hide the default LSAR location.

# Your own OpenAI-compatible server (only with llm_provider: openai).
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=

# Contact email sent with Crossref citation lookups (Crossref's "polite
# pool"). Overrides semantic_scholar.crossref_mailto in config.yaml.
# CROSSREF_MAILTO=

# Folder of your LSAR checkout, for the optional review gate.
# LSAR_HOME=

# Full path to the Rscript program, when R is not found automatically
# (psychometrics only). Same effect as r_bridge.rscript_path in config.yaml.
# EDM_ARS_RSCRIPT=
